    "updated_at": "2026-03-16T13:34:59Z",
    "body": "Hello,\n\n`MultiplePermissionsState` doesn't have a single `status` property, but it provides **other properties** to check the permissions status:\n\n- **`allPermissionsGranted`** – `true` if **all** permissions have been granted.\n- **`revokedPermissions`** – a list of permissions that are **not** granted (you can check if it's empty).\n- **`permissions`** – the full list of `PermissionState` objects, each of which **does** have a `status` property if you need per-permission info.\n- **`shouldShowRationale`** – `true` if the user should be shown a rationale.\n\n### Example usage:\n\n```kotlin\nval permissionState = rememberMultiplePermissionsState(\n    listOf(Permission.ReadStorage, Permission.WriteStorage)\n)\n\nif (permissionState.allPermissionsGranted) {\n    // All permissions are granted\n} else {\n    // Check which permissions are revoked\n    permissionState.revokedPermissions.forEach { perm ->\n        println(\"${perm.permission} is ${perm.status}\")\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**In short:** Use `permissionState.allPermissionsGranted` to check if all permissions are granted, and `permissionState.revokedPermissions` to see which ones are denied. If you need individual permission status, iterate over `permissionState.permissions` and check each one's `status` property.",
